From: Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Subject: scene: Give each output the depth limits of its display, and tell the programs (ORDER 414)

The person's SunkLimit and PoppedLimit are built on the depth libstereo-policy
gives the output's display (its kind and physical size): a headset gets more
separation, a framed 3D screen less. The windows, the wallpaper and the eye
shifts use the output's limits, and the programs that follow a surface's depth
(kde_stereo_depth_v1, version 5) are told the limits of the output the surface
mainly sits on (depth_limits), so a page's popped element and the desktop's
popped menu agree on the same screen.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
